## Afternoon: the linearity checker, built

    f508091  the checker carries diagnostic codes, not just a count
    3cf2b3a  the linear discipline: one walk, six diagnostics
    9080264  a minted owner carries the discipline too
    eb0aa14  a mutable record has one owner: consume-of and CDX2062
    4deac6d  a tuple can carry a linear component; the pattern decides

A linear value is used exactly once; a mutable record is handed to a NEW OWNER
at most once. Different rules, and the difference is the design: reading a
field of a mutable record is free, and only a call that gives it back makes a
second owner. `linear_gate.sh` 25 agree / 0 differ / 1 skipped.

`check.rs` had never carried the `mutable` keyword past the parser --
`TypeDef::Record` held the flag and nothing read it.

